  "description": "XASDUT crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C112 H100 Cl4 Dy7 N8 O36 Zn4 5+,5(Cl1 1-). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Zn1 (Zn) has 3 O neighbors; Zn2 (Zn) has 3 O neighbors; Dy1A (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2A (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy4A (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Zn1A (Zn) has 3 O neighbors; Zn2A (Zn) has 3 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 18 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.318-4.270 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 96.80-133.14°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Zn4Dy7(OH)4(O2)2(L1)8Cl4(H2O)4]Cl5. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
